  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Judge these flows. The question is: **does the path deliver the value, or only\npresent the feature?**\n\nStructure is already machine-checked. Spend your attention on the path.\n\n## The flows\n\n{{.inputs.flows}}\n\n## The patterns lifted from them\n\n{{.inputs.new_patterns}}\n\n## The deliverables they serve\n\n{{.inputs.features}}\n\n## The docs this phase reads\n\n{{.inputs.working_set}}\n\n**These are paths, not contents.** Open each one with `read_file` before you start. Read the\nfile as it is now — an earlier state in this phase may have edited it since the run began.\n\nThe pattern catalog is among them: a flow that deviates from a pattern has to justify the\ndeviation, and you cannot judge that without reading what the pattern actually says.\n\n## Findings from the previous pass\n\n{{.inputs.prior_findings}}\n\n## What to check\n\n- **Deliverables with no path**, and paths that serve no deliverable.\n- **Does the success signal match the deliverable's metric?** If the metric\n  cannot be observed anywhere along this flow, one of the two is wrong — and it\n  is usually the metric.\n- **Duplicate flows.** Are two flows the same path with different entry points?\n  Then it is one flow with two triggers, and splitting it here produces two of\n  everything downstream.\n- **Steps that serve the system.** Which step exists because the machine needs it\n  — a confirmation, a mode switch, a name it could have generated? Each is a step\n  the person did not ask for.\n- **Knowledge the actor does not have.** Walk the steps as someone who has never\n  seen this: at which step would they not know what to choose? `actor knows` is\n  the evidence.\n- **Does the error state carry them forward,** or merely inform them? A flow\n  whose error row ends the path has been labelled, not designed.\n- **Is the \"today\" path honestly described?** If the current way is not really as\n  bad as step 1 claims, phase 1 overstated the value.\n- **Deviations from a pattern** are justified; a shape now used twice was lifted.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`findings` (severity · claim · evidence · target_id), `max_severity`,\n`max_severity_rank` (blocker=3, significant=2, minor=1, note=0), and `target`:\n\n- `draft` — the path is right, the flow as written is not.\n- `explore` — the path itself is wrong, and the candidates should be re-opened.\n- `upstream` — the deliverable is the problem, not the flow. A person routes it.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5"
    },
    "input": {},
    "output": {
      "name": "output",
      "kind": "json",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "findings": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "severity",
                "claim"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "severity": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "blocker",
                    "significant",
                    "minor",
                    "note"
                  ]
                },
                "claim": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "evidence": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "A path:line, a quotation, or a reproduction."
                },
                "target_id": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "The deliverable, flow, component or unit id this is about."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "max_severity": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "blocker",
              "significant",
              "minor",
              "note"
            ]
          },
          "max_severity_rank": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "target": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "draft",
              "explore",
              "upstream"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "findings",
          "max_severity",
